& [CollisionReview] finds no unresolved hard collision
  + [collision_1] all_SOP_as_language versus not_all_SOP_as_program resolves through DocumentRole and RegionRole
  + [collision_2] compiles_straight_to_AI versus exact_first resolves through multi-target projection and SOP-N advisory status
  + [collision_3] executable_fabric versus no_implementation_authority resolves through formation now and separate implementation later
  + [collision_4] neural_net_printer versus no_weight_correctness_claim resolves through staged blueprint and experimental target evidence
  + [collision_5] self_hosting versus independent_trust resolves through explicit bootstrap root
  + [collision_6] concise_contract versus complete_dependency_accounting resolves through minimal frame selected from a complete signed dependency graph
  + [collision_7] cross_target_equivalence versus neural_nondeterminism resolves by limiting each proof to its declared observational guarantee

& [ConstraintDisposition] is phase-lock eligible
  + [hard_constraint_failure_count] is 0
  + [profile_constraint_deferred_count] is 2
  + [implementation_or_runtime_deferred_count] is 3
  + [experimental_unproven_count] is 2
  + [deferred_item_authority] is none
  + [source_revision_required] is false
  + [canonical_scope] is purpose semantics with explicit future obligations and no implementation release

& [InvalidationRule] is fail-closed
  + any hard constraint failure invalidates the purpose signature
  + a deferred implementation or experiment cannot be cited as completed proof
  + new target, effect, program-default, signature meaning, or bootstrap assumption requires fresh source and constraint reapplication
